sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/development-containers.md#create): every new Instance is a ZFS clone of the Project's default Instance on its Node. A clone's create ends when its thread is usable: the checkout, T3 and its registration (docs/reference/development-containers.md#a-clone-create-is-two-operations); its terminal projection admits `instance.complete` for the database, a nested fleet, the Processes and the Route (docs/cli/instance/complete.mmd). Built for the Nodes of the build list. The kind and its step names follow docs/cli/instance/create.mmd; the intent's `container.clone` marks a clone. The Project's first default Instance is container/create-default.mmd; when the charts move into place, it becomes the first-default branch of this chart.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:create
  %% kind: instance.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:create<br/>PROJECT NODE NAME
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:create PROJECT NODE NAME`
  %%> - syntax: `<project> <node> <name> [--root=PATH] [--domain=HOST] [--branch=BRANCH] [--database-server=SLUG] [--wait-active]`
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve Instance<br/>address · T3 port · .env
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has node access to the target Node, an active `app-dev` Node
  %%> - a Project with `nested_fleet` on is admitted only as a container in the nested Incus project: `instance.nested_fleet_host_unavailable` (409) when the Node has nested-fleet hosting off, `instance.nested_fleet_container_required` (409) when the Node is not on the build list or the result is a host checkout, both before any record; the clone is a copy of its default, in the same Incus project
  %%> - the Project's `default` Instance runs in a container on this Node, is active and has a seed snapshot, else `instance.default_missing`
  %%> - Conn is enabled, and the model router has its guard, else `operation.kind_unavailable`
  %%> - a database on a Database server clones on the default's server; another server refuses `instance.database_clone_unsupported`
  %%> - a nested-fleet Project: the Node has the nested-fleet switch, else the placement rule refuses
  %%> - a nested-fleet default whose runtime records an inner volume refuses `instance.inner_volume_clone_unavailable` (409) before any record: the clone of the volume follows separately
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Instance is reserved with its runtime record: container name, bridge address, the lowest free T3 port from 3800 and the default as clone source
  %%> - `.env` is rendered from the Project's env template; it, the placeholder model key and a repository read token go to the vault
  %%> - each attachment of the default marked shared is attached to the clone as it is (same connection, prefix and network, still shared) before `.env` renders, so `.env` holds its keys and the container intent its network path
  %%> - the clone workspace reads one private JSON vault value with `.env`, the Process environment files and the names of the keys the clone owns, of the default's connection keys, of its credential keys and of the shared connections' keys, and the default's Route host with the clone's; SSH stdin takes the whole value
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent and `container.clone`
  %%> - the Route record and the database records are reserved here, but the create publishes no Route, takes no Route publication hold and creates no database: the completion does
  %%> - the Route publication is captured as the completion will capture it and then dropped: a Route the capture refuses (for example `cluster.router_required`) refuses the create before any record
  %%> - a retained create retry records the Project's current development Processes in this admission transaction; changed definitions update their records, removed definitions remove theirs
  %%> - each Process takes its desired state from the default's copy of the same definition: stopped on the default stays stopped (installed, not started, startable by `process:start`); failed, absent or running runs
  Note over GW: Commit, push copies<br/>queue start · answer 202
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  GW->>SW: Start run from queue<br/>operation-instance-create
    SW->>N: Stage clone helpers<br/>native clone-input
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stages the release's helpers and intent from stdin in a private folder for this run; later phases run its launcher by path
    %%> - scripts and intent never fill the SSH command; the next phase keeps the repository credential on its own stdin
    SW->>N: Clone default container<br/>native clone-container
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the copy supplies the full root disk device (type, path, pool and size), whether the seed inherits it or stores it locally
    %%> - `incus copy` of the default container's snapshot `seed-<commit>`, a ZFS clone; a stopped default needs no start
    %%> - the copy gets its own bridge address and ACL, and the proxy device `t3`: NAT from the Node's WireGuard address and the T3 port to T3's port 3773
    %%> - the container's ACL lets the Node's Caddy reach port 8080, WireGuard peers reach port 3773, and the container reach its database server's port
    %%> - UFW: a route rule admits WireGuard peers to T3, below a deny for the task VM range; a rule admits the container to its database server's port
    %%> - before the first start, the stopped copy gets the Orbit root in its CA bundle when the seed's bundle lacks it, so Chromium trusts Orbit's sites; a copy without a bundle refuses
    %%> - before the first start, the stopped copy gets the composed `NO_PROXY` drop-ins, the bytes `env:sync` writes
    %%> - a nested-fleet copy starts only through the start guard: its config and devices exactly as the intent writes them, no `inner-pool` device without an inner volume in the intent, and a root volume without `zfs.delegate`
    %%> - starts the copy: nftables, `hidepid` and the image's units start; T3 does not, because `/etc/orbit/instance` does not exist yet
    %%> - right after the start, after the copy's own hosts template rewrote `/etc/hosts`: writes the plan's private names block with the renderer `env:sync` uses, so the clone resolves its own Route names; a failure is `instance.clone_private_names_failed`
    %%> Mail:
    %%> - the same launch applies the exact SMTP path before the four root-owned mail units; no separate mail playbook or step
    %%> - two IPv4 loopback sockets forward 1025 and 2525; foreign units or listeners skip setup without stopping their Process
    %%> On mail failure:
    %%> - keep a mail warning and continue workspace, T3 and registration; mail:update remains the repair command
    %%> Branch:
    %%> - fetches the Instance's branch into the Node's mirror with the read token, or creates it at the seed commit; the token stays on the Node
    opt nested-fleet clone with a Club key
      SW->>C: Deliver the Club key<br/>native clone-club-key
      %%> When: right after the copy's first start; the copy's inner Swamp serve starts with the container and reads the key from `/run/orbit-club`
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - SSH stdin into the copy's /run (a tmpfs, never a snapshot); a new key restarts the nested Gateway's Swamp serve
      %%> - the result's `nested_fleet_club_key` is what this step did; a clone that skips it says `missing`
      %%> - the inner fleet starts later, in the completion ([instance:complete](docs/cli/instance/complete.mmd))
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - `instance.nested_club_key_not_tmpfs` or `instance.nested_club_key_delivery_failed`; the checkout and T3 do not run
    end
    par checkout beside T3
    SW->>C: Check out the workspace<br/>native clone-workspace
    %%> Why beside: the T3 step never writes the workspace; T3 runs Git with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, so it takes no Git lock; the join below checks both
    %%> Why the same level: Swamp starts a level of steps only when the whole level before it has ended, in each job and across jobs; both depend on the copy and the Club key, so both start when that level ends
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - pushes the branch in as a bundle and checks it out in `/srv/workspace`; the group, setgid bits and default ACLs come with the clone
    %%> - runs only the guest's `checkout` part: the bundle, the checkout mark, `.env`; PHP settings, Process files and units are the completion's `services` part; the step keeps its name, which Conn maps to its workspace row
    %%> - after the checkout it checks the branch and commit, then writes the root-owned mark `/var/lib/orbit/workspace-checkout` with the Instance id and commit; when the mark already names this Instance, a retry skips the fetch and checkout, so the branch never moves and the result's commit stays the mark's
    %%> - writes `.env` for `orbit` with group `work`: the default's file from the seed, with the clone's own connection keys, the keys of the connections it shares with its default and `APP_URL`, without the default's other connection and Reverb keys or a copy of its credentials; `APP_KEY` stays the default's, because the cloned data is encrypted with it
    %%> - `.env` names the clone's database before the completion creates it; nothing in the container reads it before the completion starts the units
    %%> - a copied value that points at the default's Route host (its Route without a web root) points at the clone's Route host; the rest of the value stays
    %%> - prints only the names of the copied, dropped, rewritten and shared keys; the result carries them as `environment`
    %%> Task copy (`container.clone.clean_workspace`), at the first checkout, before the mark:
    %%> - excludes `/.env`, clears index flags, then `git reset --hard` and, after it, `git clean -d -ff` without `-x` until a dry run finds nothing new, with the task check's ignore rules: the default's modified and untracked files go, what the start commit's ignore rules name stays
    %%> - `git status --porcelain` must be empty, else the step fails
    %%> - the result carries the counts and the first 20 names of the reset and removed paths as `workspace_cleaned`; a clone without the mark keeps the default's tree
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - `failed_step: workspace`, `instance.create_workspace_failed`
    and T3 beside the checkout
    SW->>C: Start T3<br/>native clone-t3
    %%> When: with the checkout; a failed copy or Club key skips it, as it skips the checkout
    %%> What it does, in one step:
    %%> - the agent part: writes the placeholder key for `agent` from SSH stdin, and the Claude Code and Codex settings that point at the model forwarder
    %%> - links `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` of `agent` to the note of the Project type, and writes `/etc/orbit/instance`, owned by root and readable by all
    %%> - the T3 part: T3 starts for the first time and creates its identity; the T3 project `/srv/workspace` is added as `agent`
    %%> Check:
    %%> - waits up to 30 s for `/.well-known/t3/environment`, else `instance.t3_unready`
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - before each part the step writes the part's name to its private `t3.json`, and success removes it; on a failure or timeout `clone-session-copy` brings that file to the run, so the result keeps `failed_step: t3` with the part's code: `instance.create_agent_failed` or `instance.t3_unready`
    %%> - the Operation's failure detail is the part's own line, `instance.container_agent_failed` or `instance.container_t3_failed`, or the timeout
    %%> Why its own lock: the clone steps share one Swamp lock; T3 takes `ic-clone-t3-…`, so it runs beside the checkout
    end
    SW->>C: Register the T3 server<br/>native clone-register
    %%> When: the join; the sessions check waits for T3 and the checkout, because it checks the branch and the checkout mark
    %%> On a failed checkout: no sessions check, no registration; the container stop below still runs
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - see conn/environment-renew.mmd: the sessions go to the vault, and the step checks the environment id and scopes
    %%> - checks no Process unit: the units start in the completion, whose check refuses a dead one with `instance.container_process_inactive`
  alt all steps pass in budget
    C-->>SW: T3 answers
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Read baseline, record T3<br/>admit instance.complete
    %%> Before the transaction:
    %%> - reads the workspace baseline over SSH (`ContainerWorkspaceRead::baseline`, at most 4 s) and the T3 session from the vault; no lock waits on the network
    %%> In one transaction:
    %%> - the clone stays `source_resolved` with its `starting_commit`; the runtime is `running`; the Conn layer records the T3 server from the result
    %%> - writes `workspace_baseline` and `workspace_baseline_at`, then turns the create `succeeded`, so the baseline is older than the create's end and than any pairing
    %%> - after the create row is terminal, admits `instance.complete` with the Instance lock, so nothing takes the Instance in between; the result's `completion_operation_id` names it
    %%> - the completion's vault copy and its Swamp start run after the commit
    %%> - a completion that is refused all the same (the Route capture again, after a change to the fleet) is recorded as a failed `instance.complete` with that code, `failed_step: complete` and the recovery `instance:complete`; another error is recorded as `operation.admission_failed`; the create still succeeds and names it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the user can pair with T3 and work; the Processes, the database, a nested fleet and the Route follow in the completion
    %%> - "fully set up" is only the Instance's `status: active`, which a succeeded completion sets ([instance:complete](docs/cli/instance/complete.mmd))
    %%> - the result's `processes_stopped` names the Processes the completion installs but leaves stopped, as on the default
    %%> - the receipt includes when T3 answered and when its sessions passed
    %%> On a failed baseline read:
    %%> - the create fails with `instance.workspace_baseline_unavailable`, `failed_step: register`; the T3 server is not recorded and no completion starts
    %%> - the container keeps running; a retry of the create runs again over it, and `instance:destroy` removes it
  else Instance already created
    Note over GW: Skipped — already created<br/>instance.exists
  else a step fails or the budget ends
    C--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    SW->>N: Attempt container stop<br/>incus stop
    %%> What stays:
    %%> - the reservation, runtime, and any container, workspace and owned database records stay until the owner acts; the create made no Route publication and no database
    %%> - a refused retry removes none of them; stop is attempted; failed compensation leaves its step failed
    %%> - shared service endpoint records and rules may remain even after destroy until endpoint lifecycle work is live
    %%> - failed and cancelled creates, including cancellation before work starts, report retained_for_retry, the same create command with a new idempotency key, and forced destroy
    %%> Cleanup:
    %%> - remove the private clone folder after success or failure, beside `finish`, even if staging or the first launch failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    Note over GW: Record the failure
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it resumes on the same container
    %%> - a resume never moves a branch this Instance checked out: commits on it stay
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
  opt --wait-active
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show COMPLETION
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
    end
    CLI->>GW: instance:show INSTANCE
    GW-->>CLI: status
    %%> - exits 0 only when the Instance is `active`; any other end exits 1
  end
